				<r3d:description language="eng">ROAD is a spatio-temporal database designed to support a systemic understanding of human activities and expansions between 3 million and 20 thousand years ago (3 Ma – 20 ka) across Africa and Eurasia. It contains cultural, anthropological, environmental, and geographical information about archaeological sites and assemblages.

Open access is provided through several tools: the basic web map &#039;Simple Search&#039;, the simplified data query tool &#039;AskROAD&#039;, the &#039;Summary Data Sheets&#039;, which compile all information on a locality in a user-friendly PDF format, and &#039;roadDB&#039;, a package for data retrieval through R. After registration, full access to the database is available via a SQL query interface and the geoinformation system &#039;Map Module&#039;.</r3d:description>
